course: dictionary
lesson: 5501
title: Lawyer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A lawyer is a person whose job is to know the law, give advice about it and speak for people in court. The words around the word give clues. «A solicitor is a kind of lawyer who helps with legal things like a divorce» tells you a lawyer helps with legal things, so lawyer must mean someone who knows the law.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into a sentence. «Dad hired a good lawyer to help with his will.» If you swap in "a person who knows the law and gives advice", the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Lawyer can also be used in a playful, informal way. «You sound like a lawyer» means you argue very cleverly, not that you have a law job. The word sound shows this is a comparison, so the meaning is about how someone talks, not about a real job.
fact: Lawyer is a noun. The plural is lawyers.
fact: A lawyer is a person whose job is to know the law and give advice about it.
fact: A lawyer can speak for people in court, for example a defence lawyer who defends someone in court.
fact: A solicitor is a kind of lawyer who helps with things like wills, houses and contracts.
fact: Informally, «you sound like a lawyer» means someone argues very cleverly.
exercise: «A lawyer spoke for Mia in court.» What is a lawyer's job in this sentence? | *To speak for people in court | To drive the court bus | To cook food for the judge | To paint the walls of the court
exercise: Dad wants to hire a good lawyer to help with his will. What does lawyer mean? | A type of bird | Someone who is always late | *A person who knows the law and gives advice about it | A kind of shop
exercise: Ella says, «You argue like a lawyer.» What does this suggest? | You are very tired | You must go to court tomorrow | You are a famous judge | *You argue very cleverly
test: «A solicitor is a kind of lawyer who helps with legal things like a divorce.» What is a solicitor? | A kind of police officer | *A type of lawyer | A teacher of maths | A court cleaner
test: A defence lawyer defends someone in court. What does defends mean here? | Attacks | Hides | Falls asleep | *Speaks for and protects
exam: When someone says, «You sound like a lawyer» about an argument, what does lawyer mean? | *Someone who argues very cleverly | Someone who is always silent | A person who sells food | A kind of house
